description:
LIFECYCLE EVENT BUS (P2): Current events.rs has EventType enum with 13 variants (AgentRegistered/Started/Progress/Blocked/Completed/Failed/Crashed/Stopped/Replaced/HandoffCreated/PromptStalled/Rejected + WorkSubmitted/Verified/Accepted/Rejected/ReviewEscalated). Need comprehensive lifecycle events.

NEW EVENT TYPES:
- PeerSpawned { peer_id, pid, workspace, disposition }
- PeerReady { peer_id }
- PeerCrashed { peer_id, exit_code, signal, workspace_lease_id }
- PeerStopped { peer_id, reason }
- TaskReceived { task_id, assigned_to }
- TaskExecuting { task_id, peer_id }
- TaskCompleted { task_id, peer_id }
- TaskFailed { task_id, peer_id, error }
- VerificationStarted { task_id, profile }
- VerificationPassed { task_id, evidence_id }
- VerificationFailed { task_id, findings }
- WorkspaceAcquired { lease_id, path, holder }
- WorkspaceReleased { lease_id }
- WorkspaceCleaned { lease_id }
- LeadHandoff { from_lead, to_lead, reason }

EVENT BUS ARCHITECTURE:
- EventBus struct with handlers: HashMap<EventType, Vec<Box<dyn Handler>>>
- emit(event) → dispatch to all registered handlers
- Handler trait: fn handle(&self, event: &Event) -> Result<()>
- RecoveryHandler: on PeerCrashed → cleanup workspace
- EvidenceHandler: on VerificationPassed → persist EvidenceRecord
- NotificationHandler: on events → log to SQLite + optional webhook

FILES:
- crates/anti-core/src/events.rs — expand EventType enum
- crates/anti-daemon/src/bus.rs (NEW) — EventBus, Handler trait, built-in handlers

INTEGRATION:
- Replace direct emit_event() calls with EventBus.emit()
- Register handlers at daemon startup
- Recovery handler wired to TreehouseAdapter

Tests:
- emit PeerCrashed → RecoveryHandler called
- emit VerificationPassed → EvidenceHandler called
- emit without handler → no panic (log warning)

## Background

The daemon needs to use AntiPool instead of the old treehouse subprocess calls for workspace management. This includes pool initialization, spawn, reaper, and stop/kill flows.

## Goal

Wire AntiPool into the daemon's process lifecycle management.

## Scope

### Modified: `crates/anti-daemon/src/main.rs`

#### Pool initialization

```rust
// In daemon startup, create pool per state_dir
let pool = AntiPool::new(&state_dir, config.pool.clone());
```

#### Improved spawn

```rust
async fn spawn(&self, params: SpawnParams) -> Result<AgentRecord> {
    // 1. Validate inputs
    // 2. Reserve identity (SQLite INSERT)
    // 3. Acquire workspace from POOL (not subprocess)
    let lease = self.pool.acquire(
        &params.repo_root,
        params.remote_url.as_deref(),
        &params.id,
        params.timeout.map(Duration::from_secs),
    )?;

    // 4. Spawn agent (existing logic)
    let child = cmd.spawn()?;
    let pid = child.id();

    // 5. Attach PID with owner_started_at (PID-reuse safe)
    self.store.attach_pid_with_timestamp(&params.id, pid)?;

    // 6. Track in HashMap
    self.children.lock().unwrap().insert(params.id.clone(), child);

    Ok(record)
}
```

#### Improved reaper

```rust
// In reaper thread, release via pool on exit
fn reapExited(&mut self) {
    for (id, child) in self.children.iter_mut() {
        if let Some(status) = child.try_wait()? {
            // Release worktree via pool
            if let Some(lease) = self.store.get_lease(id) {
                let _ = self.pool.release(&lease.repo_root, lease.remote_url.as_deref(), &lease.path);
            }
            // Update status
            self.store.set_status(id, if status.success() { "Completed" } else { "Crashed" })?;
        }
    }
}
```

#### Improved stop/kill

```rust
async fn stop_agent(&self, id: &str) -> Result<()> {
    // 1. Kill process (existing logic)
    // 2. Release worktree via pool (NEW!)
    if let Some(lease) = self.store.get_lease(id) {
        let _ = self.pool.release(&lease.repo_root, lease.remote_url.as_deref(), &lease.path);
    }
    // 3. Update DB status
    self.store.set_status(id, "Stopped")?;
    Ok(())
}
```

### Modified: `crates/anti-daemon/src/peer_manager.rs`

- Wire pool through PeerManager for process lifecycle operations
- PeerManager::terminate() → kill + pool.release()

## Considerations

- The pool must be thread-safe (Arc<AntiPool> or pass by reference)
- Reaper runs in a separate thread — pool access must be safe
- Keep existing HashMap<String, Child> tracking during transition
- Graceful shutdown: pool.gc() should be called on daemon exit

## Verification

- Agent spawn → acquire → run → exit → release cycle works
- Kill agent → release worktree immediately
- Daemon restart → pool.gc() reclaims orphans
- `cargo test -p anti-daemon` passes

## Background

anti_subagent needs to implement the `TreehouseEnv` trait and a `AntiPool` wrapper to use treehouse-core as a library instead of subprocess calls. The pool lives inside `~/.anti_subagent/worktrees/`.

## Goal

Create `AntiEnv` (implements `TreehouseEnv`) and `AntiPool` (wraps `TreehouseCore<AntiEnv>`) in a new file.

## Scope

### New file: `crates/anti-workspace/src/pool.rs`

#### AntiEnv

```rust
pub struct AntiEnv {
    state_dir: PathBuf,  // ~/.anti_subagent or custom
    repo_root: PathBuf,  // set per-acquire
}

impl TreehouseEnv for AntiEnv {
    fn pool_root(&self) -> Option<PathBuf> {
        Some(self.state_dir.join("worktrees"))
    }
    fn update_cache_path(&self) -> Option<PathBuf> { None }
    fn user_config_path(&self) -> Option<PathBuf> { None }
    // All filesystem methods delegate to std::fs
}
```

#### AntiPool

```rust
pub struct AntiPool {
    core: TreehouseCore<AntiEnv>,
}

impl AntiPool {
    pub fn new(state_dir: &Path, config: PoolConfig) -> Self;
    pub fn acquire(&self, repo_root, remote_url, holder, ttl) -> Result<Lease>;
    pub fn release(&self, repo_root, remote_url, path) -> Result<bool>;
    pub fn gc(&self, repo_root, remote_url) -> Result<GcResult>;
}
```

#### PoolConfig

```rust
pub struct PoolConfig {
    pub max_trees: u32,           // default: 16
    pub lock_timeout_secs: u64,   // default: 10
    pub gc_interval_secs: u64,    // default: 300
}
```

### Modified: `crates/anti-workspace/src/lib.rs`

- Add `pub mod pool;`
- Re-export `AntiPool`, `AntiEnv`, `PoolConfig`

## Considerations

- AntiEnv must be `Send + Sync` (required by TreehouseEnv trait)
- Pool is per-repo (treehouse pools are keyed by repo + hash)
- `AcquiredWorktree` struct replaces the current `Lease` struct for library usage
- Keep existing `Lease` struct for backward compatibility

