## Context
Phase 3 of PLAN-v3-runtime-engine. Currently the daemon manages peers through Store (SQLite) and HashMap<String, Child> directly, with spawn logic split across spawn/spawn_peer/spawn_peer_impl in main.rs. This bead extracts into a proper PeerManager struct.

The PeerManager owns the lifecycle of peer processes: spawn, wait, terminate, crash detection. It does NOT own the state store or event log — those stay in main.rs behind Arc<Mutex<Store>>.

## What to build
Create `crates/anti-daemon/src/peer_manager.rs`:

```rust
pub struct PeerManager {
    children: Arc<Mutex<HashMap<String, Child>>>,
}

impl PeerManager {
    /// Spawn a peer process (no lock held during I/O)
    pub fn spawn_process(
        &self,
        spec: &SpawnSpec,
        workspace: &WorkspaceLease,
    ) -> Result<u32, SpawnError>;

    /// Check if a peer process is still alive
    pub fn is_alive(&self, id: &str) -> bool;

    /// Wait for a peer to exit
    pub fn wait(&self, id: &str) -> Result<Option<ExitStatus>>;

    /// Send SIGTERM, wait, then SIGKILL if needed
    pub fn terminate(&self, id: &str) -> Result<()>;

    /// Send SIGKILL immediately
    pub fn kill(&self, id: &str) -> Result<()>;

    /// Remove completed child handle (called by reaper)
    pub fn remove(&self, id: &str) -> Option<Child>;
}
```

## Critical: Lock discipline
Phase 0 established: NO external I/O under store Mutex. The spawn flow is already split into phases — PeerManager must preserve this:
- With lock: validate, persist metadata to store, commit results
- Without lock: treehouse acquire, process spawn, wait

PeerManager only holds the children HashMap lock. It does NOT touch the store directly.

## Reap integration
The existing reap_children background thread (5s poll, try_lock) delegates to PeerManager for:
- Process liveness check (try_wait)
- Crash detection → emit PeerCrashed event → defer Treehouse cleanup
- Exit code interpretation (≤2 = Completed, >2 = Crashed)

